TUnit has four lifecycle scopes, each with `[Before(...)]` / `[After(...)]` attributes. Here's a sketch for each:

### 1. Before/after every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ClearAsync();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsCreated() { /* ... */ }
}
```

You can also use a **constructor** or `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync` for per-test work.

---

### 2. Once per class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class CustomerApiTests
{
    private static HttpClient _client = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client = new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("http://localhost") };
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task GetCustomer_Returns200() { /* use _client */ }
}
```

> These **must be `static`** — they run once for the class, not per instance.

---

### 3. Once per assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start in-process WireMock server
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // stop server
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Once per entire test session

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseHook
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### Quick reference

| Scope | Before | After | Must be static? |
|---|---|---|---|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` | No |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` | `[After(Class)]` | **Yes** |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` | `[After(Assembly)]` | **Yes** |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` | `[After(TestSession)]` | **Yes** |

**Bonus:** `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (also `Class`, `Assembly` variants) are *global* cross-cutting hooks that fire for every test/class/assembly across the run — handy for logging or diagnostics without touching each test class. The context parameter and `CancellationToken` are optional on all hooks.
